# Runtime Dev Branch Notes — Capability Service Contract v1

**Date:** 2026-06-15  
**Branch:** `capability-service-contract-v1`  
**Status:** Repo-verified on branch and main for the declared contract-only scope; syntax-checked, contract-smoke-tested, helper-checked, artifact-guarded, and Michael-run targeted tests passed. No real-runtime test required because this branch does not touch runtime/worker/lifecycle/native execution surfaces.

---

## Purpose

This branch adds a contract-only Capability Service layer under `runtime/bus/`.

The branch answers, in code and tests:

```text
how a capability service descriptor declares a stable serviceId for a capability;
how service descriptors define input/result/cancellation/stream expectations without executing anything;
how a service registry validates and exposes service descriptors;
how a service plan checks a router plan against matching service metadata;
how service contracts remain metadata-only and non-executing.
```

This is the next substrate step after the action envelope, capability registry, bus skeleton, and capability router contract branches:

```text
action envelope -> bus intake -> router plan -> service contract -> backend adapter contract -> executor
```

