## Modular design shape

The branch follows the split router-contract pattern:

```text
capabilityServiceCommon.mjs          shared constants/copy/prefix/guard helpers
capabilityServiceDefinition.mjs      service metadata definition validation
capabilityServiceRegistry.mjs        service registry validation and lookup helpers
capabilityServicePlan.mjs            route-plan-to-service-plan validation
capabilityServiceContract.mjs        small public barrel/export surface
```

The public import surface is the barrel:

```js
import {
    assertCapabilityServiceDefinition,
    assertCapabilityServicePlan,
    assertCapabilityServiceRegistry,
    createCapabilityServiceRegistry,
    getCapabilityService,
    listCapabilityServices,
    validateCapabilityServicePlan
} from "../runtime/bus/capabilityServiceContract.mjs";
```

---

## Contract behavior summary

### Service definitions

Service definition helpers:

```text
CAPABILITY_SERVICE_CONTRACT_VERSION
CAPABILITY_SERVICE_REGISTRY_SCHEMA_VERSION
CAPABILITY_SERVICE_STATUSES
isKnownCapabilityServiceStatus()
isKnownCapabilityServiceRequirementSupportLevel()
isKnownCapabilityServiceApprovalSupportLevel()
normalizeCapabilityServiceDefinition()
validateCapabilityServiceDefinition()
assertCapabilityServiceDefinition()
copyCapabilityServiceDefinition()
```

Service definitions are metadata only. Validation requires:

```text
serviceId
capability
version
status
summary
contracts
input
result
requirements
compatibility
```

Validation rejects unknown top-level fields, unknown nested contract fields, prototype-pollution keys, execution payload keys, model/projector path keys, path-like metadata values, duplicate input/result field labels, unknown service statuses, and unknown support-level values.

### Service registry

Service registry helpers:

```text
normalizeCapabilityServiceRegistry()
validateCapabilityServiceRegistry()
assertCapabilityServiceRegistry()
createCapabilityServiceRegistry()
listCapabilityServices()
getCapabilityService()
hasCapabilityService()
```

Registry validation includes schema versioning, nested service validation, `serviceId` uniqueness, copied lookup/list results, and support for multiple service definitions for the same capability when `serviceId` disambiguates them.

### Service plans

Service plan helpers:

```text
normalizeCapabilityServicePlan()
validateCapabilityServicePlan()
assertCapabilityServicePlan()
```

Service-plan validation accepts a normalized Capability Router route plan plus a Capability Service registry, then checks:

```text
route plan wrapper contractVersion;
bus action wrapper/action/capabilityDefinition shape;
route definition shape;
service registry shape;
route.serviceId exists in the service registry;
service status is selectable;
service capability matches route capability;
service serviceId matches route serviceId;
route backendKind is allowed by service compatibility;
modelBundleId and hardwareProfileId are present when service compatibility requires them;
streaming, timeout, cancellation, and contextRefs metadata are compatible.
```

The resulting service plan is still a descriptor. It does not call a service, call a backend, enqueue a request, emit runtime events, stream tokens, or touch native/model execution.

